---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — Bolt"
  description="How Bolt and its website handle device data, local backups, appearance preferences and GitHub downloads."
>
  <main id="main" class="wrap prose">
    <span class="eyebrow">PRIVACY · OCTOBER 17, 2026</span>
    <h1>
      Your device.
      <br />
      Your data.
    </h1>
    <p>
      Bolt’s Android app has no advertising or analytics SDKs and does not
      request Android’s internet permission. Its app-owned settings, operation
      records, logs and recovery snapshots are stored locally.
    </p>
    <h2>Local files and permissions</h2>
    <p>
      Bolt uses root for privileged kernel, backup and restore operations.
      Android’s document picker grants access to the ZIPs and backup or log
      destinations you choose. Foreground-service and wake-lock permissions keep
      operations running; notification permission lets Bolt show operation
      notifications.
    </p>
    <p>
      Device identity and build information are recorded with recovery manifests
      to help validate restores. Device-bound snapshots, journals and logs are
      excluded from Android cloud backup and device transfer. They are lost if
      you clear app data or uninstall Bolt. Files you export remain wherever you
      save them.
    </p>
    <h2>Kernel packages</h2>
    <p>
      A kernel ZIP contains third-party scripts that run with root access. Those
      scripts can independently access files, modify your device or perform
      network operations. Bolt’s own lack of an internet permission does not
      restrict a root installer. Use packages from developers you trust.
    </p>
    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      This static website has no analytics, advertising scripts or cookies. If
      you change its color theme, it saves that choice in your browser’s local
      storage under <code>bolt-web-theme</code>. Fonts and screenshots are
      hosted with the site.
    </p>
    <p>
      When the download section approaches view, your browser requests the
      latest release information from GitHub’s public API. GitHub receives
      normal request information such as your IP address. Download links and
      source links also take you to GitHub. See{" "}
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">
        GitHub’s privacy statement
      </a>
      .
    </p>
    <p>
      The hosting provider serves the page and may keep standard operational
      request logs. Hosting and domain configuration are managed by the project
      owner.
    </p>
    <h2>Sharing logs and getting help</h2>
    <p>
      Exported logs can include device information and text emitted by a kernel
      installer. Review them before sharing them in a public issue. For
      questions, contact the maintainer through the{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/trinadhthatakula/Bolt">Bolt repository</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>
